  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CA CLIFF- Continuation and Widening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.   Consolidation of CLIFF India (CLIFF-1). The aim of this result is to consolidate CLIFF 1 operations in India with a view to significantly strengthening scalability.  2.   Upscaling CLIFF Kenya (CLIFF-2). The aim of this result is to demonstrate and build a mechanism for financing housing and settlement development for the urban poor in Kenyacomma through which Muungano wa Wanavijiji will have space to learn and build effective demand; partnerships are built with city authorities and national policy makers; andcomma other actors are drawn into financing housing and settlement development for the urban poor. 3.   Setting up a CLIFF-3. Set up a third sustainable CLIFF in another country that fully complies with the principles and conditionalities for being such a facility 4.   Creation of an Urban Poor Global Fund. Conceptualisecomma design andcomma if appropriatecomma capitalise by March 2008comma an Urban Poor Fund aimed at creating a facility to empower urban poor communities to negotiate with their cities for landcomma housing and infrastructure. The purpose is: 1.   The design of a global facility 2.   Innovative methods for urban poor to negotiate 3.   Need for collective action for effective access to resources</narrative>
  </description>
